<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sajó</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Slaná</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Sajó, Slovak Slaná, is a river about 230 kilometres long that rises in the Slovak <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ore-mountains">Ore Mountains</a> and flows south-east through north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a> to join the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tisza">Tisza</a>. On its banks near the village of Muhi the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a> destroyed the army of Béla IV at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-mohi">Battle of Mohi</a> in April 1241.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sajo.jpg" alt="Sajó" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Marosvari.gergo · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Saj%C3%B3_l%C3%A1tk%C3%A9pe.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
